<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad bin Thani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1788–<a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad bin Thani was the leader of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doha">Doha</a> and the first ruler of Qatar recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. After a destructive war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> and Abu Dhabi, he signed an agreement with the British envoy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewis-pelly">Lewis Pelly</a> in 1868 that treated him as the peninsula's leader and separated Qatar from Bahraini claims. His son Jassim, who succeeded him, is regarded as the founder of the Qatari state.</p></div>
